# NOTE: pub uses this file INSTEAD of .gitignore when deciding what goes into the
# published archive — it does not add to it. Every build output .gitignore keeps
# out of git therefore has to be repeated here, or it ships. This is not
# theoretical: `flutter test` leaves two ~46 MB kernel caches under
# build/test_cache/, and publishing from a working tree put both in the archive,
# taking it from 117 KB to 29 MB.
#
# Publishing is irreversible, so check the `--dry-run` file list before pushing a
# version up.

# Build outputs, at any depth — this covers example/build/ as well as ./build/.
build/
coverage/
Pods/
.symlinks/

# Not the example's, which pub.dev renders as the Example tab.
/pubspec.lock

# Development tooling that consumers of the package have no use for. The example
# is deliberately NOT excluded — pub.dev renders it as the package's Example tab.
#
# test/ goes too, and not only for size: some of it imports tool/, which is
# excluded here, so shipping the tests would put dangling imports in the archive
# for pub.dev's analysis to trip over.
.github/
test/
tool/
renovate.json
.pre-commit-config.yaml
CLAUDE.md
